<title>USA: Rep. Leach praises Fed move on bank underwriting.</title>
<headline>Rep. Leach praises Fed move on bank underwriting.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rep. Jim Leach, chairman of the House Banking Committee, praised the Federal Reserve's decision on Friday to allow banks to expand their securities underwriting activities.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's Federal Reserve action represents a progressive step forward in providing consumers a more competitive financial marketplace,&quot; the Iowa Republican said in a statement.</p>
<p>Leach said Tuesday that he would propose a more comprehensive reform of the nation's financial services industry regulation. --Aaron Pressman ((202-898-8312))</p>
